<title>EGYPT: Egypt, Poland sign security cooperation accord.</title>
<headline>Egypt, Poland sign security cooperation accord.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-10-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt and Poland signed a security accord on Saturday aimed at coordinating their efforts to fight organised crime and terrorism, Egypt's interior ministry said.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that Egyptian Ministry of Interior Hassan el-Alfi and his Polish counterpart, Zbigniew Siemiatkowski, signed the accord in Cairo.</p>
<p>It aims to boost cooperation and exchange of information between the two countries on fighting organised crime, terrorism, drug smuggling and forgery, the statement said.</p>
</text>
